member.param:
This parameter specifies the device to be initialized (Resource Name). The syntax for this parameter is:
ITC5000: USB0::0x1313::0x8081::DEVICE-SERIAL-NUMBER::INSTR
For remote VISA sessions use. VISA://HOSTNAME[:PORT]/ as a prefix. Where HOSTNAME is the name of the machine running the VISA server and PORT is the TCP port of the VISA server.
Note: You may use VISA <Find Resources> to get the Resource Name for your device. Use the search patterns below for <Find Resources>.
ITC5000: USB Interface USB?*INSTR{VI_ATTR_MANF_ID==0x1313 && VI_ATTR_MODEL_CODE==0x8281} ETH Interface TCPIP?*:INSTR{VI_ATTR_TCPIP_DEVICE_NAME==\"ITC5000\" || VI_ATTR_TCPIP_DEVICE_NAME==\"ITC5252\"}
LDC5000 (As StandAlon device) ASRL?*::INSTR{VI_ATTR_MANF_ID==0x1313 && VI_ATTR_MODEL_CODE==0x8283}
TED5000 (As StandAlon device) ASRL?*::INSTR{VI_ATTR_MANF_ID==0x1313 && VI_ATTR_MODEL_CODE==0x8282}
